From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Alexander M. Merritt" <alexander@edera.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:18:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/virt: add an option to keep the firmware's PCI
 configuration

Without _DSM function 5 on the host bridge, an arm64 Linux assigns
every BAR and bridge window again. Graviton's firmware provides it,
so Linux there keeps the firmware's layout, and Xen relies on that:
it hides its console UART from dom0 and makes the port above it
read-only, which dom0's new layout would overlap. The virt machine
already builds that _DSM, but only for an accelerated SMMUv3, which
needs KVM. Let the user ask for it, so that a boot test under TCG
sees Graviton's layout.

Signed-off-by: Alexander M. Merritt <alexander@edera.dev>
---
 hw/arm/virt.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/virt.c b/hw/arm/virt.c
index 219597cabd..5a303753e0 100644
--- a/hw/arm/virt.c
+++ b/hw/arm/virt.c
@@ -3518,6 +3518,21 @@ static void virt_set_dtb_randomness(Object *obj, bool value, Error **errp)
     vms->dtb_randomness = value;
 }
 
+static bool virt_get_pci_preserve_config(Object *obj, Error **errp)
+{
+    VirtMachineState *vms = VIRT_MACHINE(obj);
+
+    return vms->pci_preserve_config;
+}
+
+static void virt_set_pci_preserve_config(Object *obj, bool value,
+                                         Error **errp)
+{
+    VirtMachineState *vms = VIRT_MACHINE(obj);
+
+    vms->pci_preserve_config = value;
+}
+
 static char *virt_get_oem_id(Object *obj, Error **errp)
 {
     VirtMachineState *vms = VIRT_MACHINE(obj);
@@ -4331,6 +4346,14 @@ static void virt_machine_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, const void *data)
     object_class_property_set_description(oc, "dtb-kaslr-seed",
                                           "Deprecated synonym of dtb-randomness");
 
+    object_class_property_add_bool(oc, "x-pci-preserve-config",
+                                   virt_get_pci_preserve_config,
+                                   virt_set_pci_preserve_config);
+    object_class_property_set_description(oc, "x-pci-preserve-config",
+                                          "Set on to tell the OS to keep the "
+                                          "PCI configuration that the "
+                                          "firmware made at boot");
+
     object_class_property_add_str(oc, "x-oem-id",
                                   virt_get_oem_id,
                                   virt_set_oem_id);
